  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Brian Thomas Moynihan (born October 9, 1959) is an American lawyer and banker. He was the chairman, president, and CEO of Bank of America, having been promoted to these positions in 2010.\nMoynihan is a member of the Council on Competitiveness board and Partnership for Rhode Island board, among other boards. He became the Chancellor of Brown University in July 2024.",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
